---
import Swap from '../../layouts/Swap.astro';
---
<Swap title="Swap B · Copydesk">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Client-side navigation</p>
      <h1>Swap page B</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width:60ch;">
        You arrived here through a body swap. The admin bar, the hover pill and
        the element tree should all still be here, edit mode should still be on
        if it was on when you left, and this heading should be editable without
        a reload.
      </p>
      <p>
        Going back with the browser's own Back button is the other half of the
        check — <code>popstate</code> is a swap the router does not announce
        with <code>astro:page-load</code> on every Astro version.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/swap/a">← Back to swap page A</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Swap>
